--- Fires after vanilla input polling when a gamepad POV hat changes. Includes joysticks enumerated by vanilla DirectInput and requires the game to initialize those devices. This observes raw state changes, including state resets when acquisition fails. It does not block game input.
--- @class gamepadPovEventData
--- @field claim boolean If set to `true`, any lower-priority event callbacks will be skipped. Returning `false` will set this to `true`.
--- @field gamepad integer *Read-only*. The zero-based gamepad ID.
--- @field isCentered boolean *Read-only*. True when the POV hat is centered (no direction is pressed).
--- @field pov integer *Read-only*. The zero-based POV hat ID, from 0 to 3.
--- @field previousValue number *Read-only*. The clockwise angle in degrees from the preceding input poll. When wasCentered is true, this is 0 and does not represent a direction.
--- @field value number *Read-only*. Clockwise angle in degrees, from 0 up to but not including 360. North is 0, east is 90, south is 180, and west is 270. When isCentered is true, this is 0 and does not represent a direction.
--- @field wasCentered boolean *Read-only*. True when the POV hat was centered in the preceding input poll.
